{"author":{"id":"2462ded6f56967dde059994c39a506c79e39e5dfd10c5a07f07a23a5652a8353"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1776783862,"nonce":"kJC8AXH+md8YYXZrSl2uQ8bBOdA=","title":"Codex sessions don't report usage/cost - turn.completed event not captured","message":"## Problem\n\nCodex sessions complete with zero usage:\n```json\n{\"input_tokens\": 0, \"output_tokens\": 0, \"cost_usd\": 0.0, \"model\": \"\"}\n```\n\n## Root cause\n\nWhen codex emits `@@DONE@@` via agent_message (item.completed), SessionRunner detects the marker and terminates the session BEFORE the `turn.completed` event (which contains usage data) is emitted by codex.\n\nEvidence from leanaider session a6915cb973d8:\n- Last event: `item.completed` with `agent_message` containing `@@DONE@@`\n- No `turn.completed` event in raw-output.log\n- Usage in state.json is all zeros\n\n## Expected behavior\n\nUsage/cost should be captured from `turn.completed` events even when session ends via @@DONE@@ marker.\n\n## Tests\n\n- tests/test_codex_agent.py::test_usage_captured_before_done_marker\n  Assert: When @@DONE@@ is in agent_message, wait for turn.completed and extract usage\n- tests/test_codex_agent.py::test_usage_from_turn_completed_after_mcp_done\n  Assert: When @@DONE@@ via MCP signal, still capture turn.completed usage\n\n## Files\n\n- adapters/agents/codex.py (modify - buffer turn.completed usage)\n- core/session.py (modify - don't terminate until turn.completed received, or extract usage on termination)\n\n## Implementation options\n\n1. **Buffer approach**: CodexAgent buffers the last turn.completed usage and SessionRunner extracts it on @@DONE@@\n2. **Wait approach**: SessionRunner waits briefly after @@DONE@@ for turn.completed before terminating\n3. **Drain approach**: On @@DONE@@, drain remaining stdout until EOF or timeout, capture any turn.completed\n\nREQ: REQ-032 (usage tracking)","files":null}]}